      "content": "Framing it as a \"controlled test of a new data handling protocol\" introduces significant risk of future discovery contradicting the narrative. This spin could easily be exposed, leading to more severe accusations of deceit from stakeholders and regulators. It is generally safer to acknowledge a minor, contained *operational update* that required an immediate, successful security patch rather than pretending a leak was a test.",
